\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years. In 2025, September to October came in at 45% of normal on the middle of the grids, and July to August hit 148%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 193% on the middle of the grids. Grid 26863 had its driest year in 2021 at 67%.</p>"}
